# BotShieldFlagTrigger — illustrative reference for the compiled-in
# default rule set.
#
# This file is NOT a required include. mod_botshield ships these
# rules compiled into the module and seeds them into every server
# scope at post_config time, so the module Just Works with zero
# config. The file exists only so operators who want to see the
# defaults can read them in a familiar httpd.conf shape, and so
# operators tweaking behavior have a starting template.
#
# To extend: add `BotShieldFlagTrigger` lines to your vhost or
# server config. Score actions accumulate (SUM); tier_floor actions
# take MAX (strictest tier wins). Operator declarations append
# after the defaults — they don't replace them unless you use the
# `reset` keyword on a per-flag basis.
#
# Syntax:
#   BotShieldFlagTrigger <flag_name> [reset] [action=<verb> args...]
#
# Action verbs:
#   action=score add=N             (signed; SUM across matching triggers)
#   action=tier_floor min=<tier>   (pass|silent|form|captcha; MAX)
#
# Reset keyword (clears earlier entries — defaults AND prior operator
# lines — for the same flag, processed at config-load time):
#   BotShieldFlagTrigger <flag> reset                              # bare
#   BotShieldFlagTrigger <flag> reset action=<verb> ...            # +inline
#   BotShieldFlagTrigger <flag> reset                              # multi-
#   BotShieldFlagTrigger <flag> action=...                         # line
#
# Observe-mode (logs `would-flag-trigger:<flag>:observe` instead of
# applying the side effect — useful for safe rollout of a new rule):
#   BotShieldFlagTrigger <flag> action=score add=N mode=observe

# --- Detection signals — definitive ---------------------------------
# Honeypot hits and fake-bot signatures (UA claims a search-engine
# crawler from a non-search-engine network, etc.) are essentially
# never legitimate traffic. Push the score and force captcha so the
# response stops short of any user content.
BotShieldFlagTrigger honeypot_hit          action=score      add=60
BotShieldFlagTrigger honeypot_hit          action=tier_floor min=captcha
BotShieldFlagTrigger fake_bot              action=score      add=80
BotShieldFlagTrigger fake_bot              action=tier_floor min=captcha

# --- Detection signals — probable -----------------------------------
# Scanner probes (vulnerability-scan path patterns) are usually bots
# but occasionally legitimate research traffic. Push score and
# require a form-PoW solve — strong friction without the captcha
# accessibility cost.
BotShieldFlagTrigger scanner_probe         action=score      add=50
BotShieldFlagTrigger scanner_probe         action=tier_floor min=form

# --- Detection signals — accumulating -------------------------------
# Repeat PoW failures from one cookie. Could be a broken client
# (JS disabled, time-skewed, CSP-stripped) or a scripted attacker
# trying to brute the challenge. Bump to silent — the next solve
# proves human behavior cheaply, and the score addition primes
# the request near the tier-bump threshold.
BotShieldFlagTrigger pow_fail_streak       action=score      add=30
BotShieldFlagTrigger pow_fail_streak       action=tier_floor min=silent

# --- Trust signals (credits) ----------------------------------------
# Application-issued reputation. The app sees session-bound state
# the module can't (logged-in user, prior good behavior, etc.) and
# feeds back via the X-BotShield-Feedback header surface. Credits
# subtract score; they never RAISE tier — a credit shouldn't force
# a request UP. Multiple credits compose additively (SUM).
BotShieldFlagTrigger app_verified_human    action=score      add=-80
BotShieldFlagTrigger app_verified_session  action=score      add=-40
BotShieldFlagTrigger app_trust_signal      action=score      add=-20

# --- Common overrides -----------------------------------------------
#
# Soften captcha to form on honeypot_hit (e.g., behind a CDN where
# captcha is troublesome):
#   BotShieldFlagTrigger honeypot_hit reset action=score add=60
#   BotShieldFlagTrigger honeypot_hit       action=tier_floor min=form
#
# Disable pow_fail_streak escalation entirely (e.g., when running
# behind a JS-restricting client that legitimately fails the PoW):
#   BotShieldFlagTrigger pow_fail_streak reset
#
# Stronger app credit (push score down 120 instead of 80):
#   BotShieldFlagTrigger app_verified_human action=score add=-40
#   # combined effect: -80 (default) + -40 (operator) = -120
#
# Try a new rule in observe-mode for one release before enforcing:
#   BotShieldFlagTrigger scanner_probe action=tier_floor min=captcha mode=observe
#   # logs `would-flag-trigger:scanner_probe:observe` on every fire;
#   # remove `mode=observe` once the rate looks right.
